"""
Scripted history: the things that happen on a date whether or not the house is
ready for them.

Each event has a year (it fires on the first turn whose span includes that
year), a title and text, an effect the engine applies, and a provenance. Most
are HISTORICAL: the date and the shape of the shock are real, and the text
says what actually happened. The magnitudes — how much of a prince's loan is
lost, how much panic a crisis adds — are STYLISED game dials.

Effect types the engine understands:

  sovereign_default  {sovereign, haircut}            loans to that prince take the haircut
  forced_loan        {sovereign, share, yield}       the state takes a share of deposits as a loan
  shock              {kind, size, cities?}           trade / property / markets / plague loss, scaled by class sensitivity
  panic              {size, cities?}                 withdrawal pressure this turn
  rule               {field, value}                  overwrites an era rule from now on
  centre             {city}                          the centre of gravity moves
  city               {city, field, value}            a city's state changes (sacked, opens, prosperity)
  regime             {id}                            a capital regime comes into force
  tech_gate          {tech, available}               a tech's availability changes (Bubble Act)
  offer              {sovereign, size, yield, turns} a prince asks for a loan — the player decides
  flavour            {}                              text only
  lifeboat           {}                              the clearers' rescue: a one-off liquidity line at a price
"""

